=== 0. build ===================================================
built.

=== 1. harness self-tests ======================================
SipCon64 harness self-tests
  reference is the p^10/p^6 schedule                             ok
  256-bit state, 64-bit rate                                     ok
  key / nonce / tag are 128 bits each                            ok
  p^12 of the zero state matches the pinned vector               ok
  AEAD encrypt matches the pinned ciphertext and tag             ok
  p^12 != p^6 o p^6 (tail schedule, not a shared prefix)         ok
  p^r moves the state for every r = 1..12                        ok
  a one-bit input change reaches p^6                             ok
  bit indexing: bit 200 is bit 8 of x3                           ok
  bit indexing: bits 0..63 are x0, the rate word                 ok
  first ciphertext block is rate XOR plaintext                   ok
  the duplex absorbs C, so later blocks are plaintext-dependent  ok
  AEAD round-trips (200 random messages)                         ok
  AEAD rejects a single-bit ciphertext/tag flip                  ok
  harness PRNG is not degenerate                                 ok

all self-tests passed (0 failure(s))

=== 2. validate the SP 800-22 implementation ===================
validating the SP 800-22 implementation (32 sequences x 1000000 bits, alpha=0.01)

control stream         expect  sub-tests  failed    exp  suite  verdict
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
os.urandom             PASS          188       4   1.06  PASS   ok
all-zero bytes         FAIL          162     162   0.66  FAIL   ok
64-bit counter         FAIL          162     161   0.66  FAIL   ok
LCG low byte           FAIL          188     188   0.77  FAIL   ok
SipCon64 p^1 (ctr)     FAIL          162     161   0.66  FAIL   ok

p-value uniformity on os.urandom (the assumption the whole two-level
assessment rests on):
  sub-tests                      188
  mean pass proportion           0.9883 (expected ~0.99)
  uniformity P_T < 0.0001        1

validation passed: the suite accepts the CSPRNG, rejects all four weak streams
including a 1-round SipCon64, and its p-values are uniform on random input.

